WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:05.279
Cheers ran from 1982 to 1993, and was one
of the biggest critical and ratings success

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:06.620
stories of its era.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:11.349
Emmy voters nominated it for Outstanding Comedy
Series in all 11 of its seasons, and Cheers

00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:15.719
ultimately won 28 Emmys against 179 total
nominations.

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:18.450
More than 40 million households watched the
show's finale.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:22.990
Still, the show's most impressive accomplishment
might be the way its stars defied typecasting

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:24.360
and have continued to find work in Hollywood.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:28.021
But while you've certainly seen them over
the years, you might not recognize the Cheers

00:00:28.021 --> 00:00:29.430
cast today…

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.080
Ted Danson - Sam Malone

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.910
After Sam Malone turned out the lights on
Cheers, Ted Danson made guest appearances

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.620
as Malone on Frasier and The Simpsons, but
went on to compete with Woody Harrelson for

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.130
the most diverse career among former cast
members.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:45.550
He played himself in 13 episodes of Curb Your
Enthusiasm, starred in the sitcom Becker for

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.500
six seasons, got another Emmy nod for his
ruthless CEO character on Damages, and appeared

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.010
on CSI: Cyber as D.B.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.690
Russell, a character he originated on CSI.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:58.489
Through all that, he's also popped up in numerous
other film and television roles, and has been

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:01.260
married to Mary Steenburgen since 1995.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:05.039
While he doesn't exactly look like bar owner
Sam Malone anymore, you can catch Danson on

00:01:05.039 --> 00:01:09.039
NBC's The Good Place and season two of FX's
Fargo.

00:01:09.039 --> 00:01:10.609
Shelley Long - Diane Chambers

00:01:10.609 --> 00:01:14.670
For five years, Diane Chambers, a Bennington
College graduate, wanted everyone to know

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.450
she was smarter than her cocktail waitress
job would indicate.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:22.229
But before season six, Shelly Long left Cheers
to pursue other work and spend more time with

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:23.229
her family.

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:26.220
"If I go, I am never, ever coming back."

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:30.179
She went on to appear in several movies and
TV shows, including The Money Pit, The Brady

00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:34.529
Bunch Movie, Troop Beverly Hills, and later
even revived Diane for an episode of Frasier.

00:01:34.529 --> 00:01:38.219
She's also been seen occasionally on Modern
Family playing DeDe Pritchett.

00:01:38.219 --> 00:01:39.799
Kirstie Alley - Rebecca Howe

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:43.920
After replacing Shelley Long on Cheers as
the new object of Sam Malone's affection,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.850
Kirstie Alley went on to star in Veronica's
Closet for three seasons and in the Look Who's

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.069
Talking movies with John Travolta.

00:01:50.069 --> 00:01:54.170
Her pseudo-reality series Fat Actress outlined
her public struggles with her weight.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:58.399
More recently she starred in one season of
her TV Land sitcom Kirstie, guest-starred

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:02.990
on the Netflix series Flaked, and been a fan
favorite on season 15 of Dancing With the

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:03.990
Stars.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.490
John Ratzenberger - Cliff Clavin

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:09.429
According to his website, John Ratzenberger
originally read for the role of Norm, but

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:12.670
sensed he wouldn't get it and suggested that
Cheers should have a know-it-all character

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:13.670
at the bar.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:17.290
The producers agreed, so they created Cliff
Clavin to drop some knowledge on us.

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:22.920
"By my calculations, the next president has
to be named Yelnik McWawa"

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:28.939
While he still works consistently as a character
actor, Ratzenberger's face isn't on camera

00:02:28.939 --> 00:02:30.129
as much as his former castmates.

00:02:30.129 --> 00:02:34.230
You've certainly heard him, though: he's Hamm
the Piggy Bank from the Toy Story movies,

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.940
and he's the only voice actor to appear in
every Pixar film.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.719
"I'll have you know that tampering with the
mail is a crime punishable by banishment!"

00:02:41.719 --> 00:02:43.959
George Wendt - Norm Peterson

00:02:43.959 --> 00:02:47.739
Wendt's acting resume since leaving Norm on
the barstool at Cheers is longer than a master

00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:49.090
mixologist's drink menu.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:53.269
In addition to his ill-fated sitcom The George
Wendt Show, he's appeared in everything from

00:02:53.269 --> 00:02:57.340
Michael Jackson's "Black or White" video to
Saturday Night Live's recurring "Da Bears"

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:01.209
sketch to comedy nerd favorites like Children's
Hospital and Portlandia .

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:03.140
Rhea Perlman - Carla Tortelli

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:07.390
After winning four Emmy awards for playing
Cheers' brash cocktail waitress, Rhea Perlman

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:09.599
has worked consistently since the show ended.

00:03:09.599 --> 00:03:13.610
She's regularly guest starred on television
shows, including The Mindy Project, and has

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:17.370
appeared in several movies, including There
Goes the Neighborhood, Sunset Park, and Matilda—

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:20.590
—the last of which co-starred her husband,
Danny DeVito.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.290
Woody Harrelson - Woody Boyd

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:26.819
The part of Woody, a small-town hayseed trying
to make it in Boston, earned Woody Harrelson

00:03:26.819 --> 00:03:30.120
five Emmy nominations, one win, and made him
a star.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.060
He rode his Cheers fame into diverse roles
in blockbuster movies like White Men Can't

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:39.280
Jump, Indecent Proposal, Natural Born Killers,
Zombieland, The People vs. Larry Flynt, and

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.739
The Messenger, the latter two of which earned
him Oscar nominations.

00:03:41.739 --> 00:03:47.430
Since then, he's starred in HBO's first season
of True Detective and The Hunger Games films.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.719
Kelsey Grammer - Dr. Frasier Crane

00:03:49.719 --> 00:03:54.239
Producers originally hired Kelsey Grammer
to appear in six-episode arc, but fans loved

00:03:54.239 --> 00:03:58.349
Frasier so much that Grammer went on to portray
the stuffy doctor for two decades.

00:03:58.349 --> 00:04:02.959
Frasier became one of the most popular TV
spinoffs of all time, running for 11 seasons

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:06.549
and winning 37 Emmy Awards against 108 nominations.

00:04:06.549 --> 00:04:10.650
Grammer has appeared often on Broadway since
Frasier ended, has made multiple guest appearances

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.969
on TV shows like 30 Rock, starred in four
more TV series that haven't been as successful

00:04:14.969 --> 00:04:19.490
including Boss and Hank, and became another
TV mainstay as Sideshow Bob on The Simpsons.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.870
And if that wasn’t enough, there was also
the time this happened.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:26.480
"It was a small world, pretending I was a
UN interpreter…

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.480
oh god!"

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.480
Thanks for watching!

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.870
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.500
And leave us a comment to let us know which
Cheers cast member is your favorite...

